          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">The earliest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neolithic">Neolithic</a> settlements known in the area belong to the Majiabang culture (5000 to 3300 BCE); Shanghai was made a market town in 1074 and the seat of a county in the early 1290s.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the southern estuary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze River</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s east coast, on a flat alluvial plain bisected by the Huangpu River, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhejiang">Zhejiang</a> to the south and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jiangsu">Jiangsu</a> to the west and north.</span></div>
